From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fe14 <engine@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:42:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/21] frontend: Fire Emblem Fates' Randomizer page after the
 New Game mode pick

The Fates port's owner asked (its docs/DECISIONS.md F-044) for the
randomizer settings as a page inside the game, right after Casual or
Classic, and a Randomizer entry in the Esc menu.

- rando_page: the form (every row the port's rando.py schema gives,
  Randomizer off by default, seed with Random, Everything on, Defaults),
  shown over the paused game when the core says the mode was picked.
  Start game hands the answers to the core; a failure offers Back or the
  original game. The schema is asked once per Fates start, in a thread,
  through Python started hidden (CREATE_NO_WINDOW, stdin closed, output
  piped into the log); never in headless runs.
- Esc menu: Randomizer (Fates only) opens This run: on/off, the seed,
  the settings not at their default, the spoiler log, the core's notices.
- rando_link: the page's only door to zakuro-core fates_rando_session
  (one data folder, one run folder, one state sidecar writer). With a
  window the core waits for the page; headless runs answer by themselves.
- <data>/rando/last.json is written only when a randomized game starts.
- --headless plays ZAKURO_REPLAY's inputs back too (it pressed nothing
  before), so a test run gets past the title by itself.
- settings test a_first_run_has_the_fates_port_picks compares another
  game's resolved settings without the per-game maps that hold Fates'
  own picks (it failed since 0006).

Our own code and words; no game data.
